    "request_text": "[{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"<session_context>\\nThis is the Gemini CLI. We are setting up the context for our chat.\\nToday's date is Friday, November 20, 2026 (formatted according to the user's locale).\\nMy operating system is: linux\\nThe project's temporary directory is: /home/jarvis/.gemini/tmp/agent\\n- **Workspace Directories:**\\n  - /home/jarvis/Desktop/Ghidramcp/agent\\n- **Directory Structure:**\\n\\nShowing up to 200 items (files + folders).\\n\\n/home/jarvis/Desktop/Ghidramcp/agent/\\n├───.gemini/\\n│   └───settings.json\\n└───logs/\\n    ├───.gitkeep\\n    └───telemetry.log\\n\\n\\n<loaded_context>\\n<project_context>\\nThe following are instructions provided by the tool server 'ghidra':\\n---[start of server instructions]---\\nTools for reverse engineering the program open in Ghidra. Call get_program_info first to confirm\\nwhich binary you are working on. Addresses are hex strings such as \\\"0x401000\\\". List tools are\\npaginated: pass offset/limit and check has_more. Prefer the address-based tools for modifications,\\nsince function names can be ambiguous.\\n\\n---[end of server instructions]---\\n</project_context>\\n</loaded_context>\\n</session_context>\"},{\"text\":\"Using only the Ghidra MCP tools, list the functions in the loaded binary, decompile main and every function it calls, then explain what input the program accepts. Name each tool you call.\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I am calling `mcp_ghidra_get_program_info` to inspect the target binary, and `mcp_ghidra_list_functions` to retrieve the list of functions.\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"mcp_ghidra_get_program_info\",\"args\":{},\"id\":\"call_1916384253871927416\"},\"thoughtSignature\":\"\"},{\"functionCall\":{\"name\":\"mcp_ghidra_list_functions\",\"args\":{\"offset\":0,\"limit\":100},\"id\":\"call_1916384253871929595\"}}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"parts\":[{\"functionResponse\":{\"id\":\"call_1916384253871927416\",\"name\":\"mcp